From: OrcaXR Android port
Subject: [PATCH] bbs_3mf: virtual-filament-aware max_filament_id clamp (Phase F.3)

Replace the `filament_settings_id`-size-only fallback in
`load_bbs_3mf`'s per-object/per-volume `extruder` clamp with the
mixed-filament-aware helper Snapmaker fork ships on
`feature_mix_filament_sm`. The helper consults `filament_colour`,
`filament_settings_id`, `filament_ids`, `default_filament_colour`,
and `nozzle_diameter` (in that priority) for the physical count, then
asks `MixedFilamentManager` to expand that to include any virtual
mixed filaments declared via `mixed_filament_definitions`.

**Why land this on Android even though it's a near-no-op today:**

`mixed_filament_definitions` rarely loads on Android because
libslic3r's `_extract_project_config_from_archive` writes a temp file
to `Model::get_backup_path()` under a non-writable mount (see
GEMINI.md gotcha #10b). The Kotlin-side `nativeRead3mfMixedFilamentDefinitions`
in `slic3r_jni.cpp` covers that path with a direct miniz reader.
However:

1. The helper still **improves the fallback** even without virtual
   filaments: `filament_settings_id` isn't always present in the
   embedded project config (Bambu Studio 3MFs sometimes drop it),
   leaving the prior code at `INT_MAX` and skipping the clamp
   entirely. The new helper also consults `filament_colour` and
   `nozzle_diameter`, both of which OrcaXR injects into every
   slice via `mergedConfig`.
2. **Lays infrastructure for Phase F.2** — when the engine emission
   port lands, this helper is what its CallSite uses to validate
   per-object filament references.

The recovery target on overflow stays at slot **1** (matching our
existing v2.3.2 behavior), not Snapmaker's slot **0**, to avoid
shifting the dragon autotest baseline. Snapmaker's `0` semantically
means "use the plate default extruder" and is the cleaner choice;
deferred so this patch is a pure cap-improvement rather than a
behavior change.

Source for the two helpers: byte-identical (modulo comment
header) to Snapmaker `feature_mix_filament_sm` HEAD `475aa05`,
`bbs_3mf.cpp` lines 578–621. Same code in FullSpectrum v0.9.8.

Depends on patch 0015 (MixedFilament.{cpp,hpp}) for
`MixedFilamentManager` symbol.

